    "_help": [
      "The mod ignores anything starting with _ (like this).",
      "Each feature has:",
      "  disabled        true = greyed out in the menu with a DISABLED tag. The feature does not run.",
      "  disabled_reason text shown when hovering DISABLED. Empty = 'This feature is currently under maintenance.'",
      "  killed          true = removed from the menu completely. The feature does not run. Beats disabled.",
      "  tooltip         text for the little 'i' next to the feature's name. Empty = no 'i'.",
      "  beta            true = show the small BETA tag, false = hide it. Leave it out = the mod's built-in choice. (1.0.2+)",
      "  versions        extra rules for specific mod versions, e.g.",
      "                  \"1.0.2\" exact | \"<1.0.4\" below | \">=1.0.2 <1.0.5\" range | \"1.0.2, 1.0.3\" either",
      "For disabled/killed the top-level settings apply to EVERY version and ALWAYS win: versions can",
      "only add a disable/kill, never turn one back on.",
      "For tooltip and beta it's the other way round: a version's value REPLACES the top-level one on that version.",
      "mod_only_sounds, slot_locking and keybinds only support tooltip and beta (they have no kill switch).",
      "announcements has no card in the menu: disabled or killed stops /announce messages reaching players (1.0.2+). Tooltip and beta do nothing for it.",
      "super_jump's tooltip is the 'i' next to Super Jump inside the Keybinds card.",
      "harvestable_<name> (whisperleaf, plain_fiber, coarse_fiber, apple, mushroom, kelp, tanglewood_vine, driftstone, cobweb) switches one harvestable off; harvestable_highlighter the whole feature.",
      "issued and features_v2.json.sig are filled in by the Sign features_v2.json GitHub Action on every push. Do not edit them by hand. 1.0.2+ builds only trust this file when the signature checks out.",
      "A feature that is missing here works normally with its built-in tooltip and beta tag.",
      "Announcements are no longer set here: use /announce in the Isles+ Discord (1.0.2+)."
    ],

